Review comment:

- [P1] Restore page content if hydration fails after bootstrap — /Users/asmirnou/Projects/g/ramsider/app/[locale]/layout.tsx:14-14
  If a Next.js script loads but throws before `PageMediaGate` hydrates, the inline bootstrap leaves `data-media-js` set. CSS then hides the server-rendered artwork and page content indefinitely, while the fallback only handles script network errors. The page gate needs a fallback for hydration failures so the static page remains readable, as required by [the media-loading plan](docs/media-loading-plan.md#work-sequence-and-gates).
